# UniPlus UI and content rule

This repository is maintained by subject teachers and teaching assistants.
Keep work inside teaching content, browser-only tools, or shared UI. If a
request changes product integrations, stop and ask the technical owner.

## Minimal implementation

- Inspect the nearest existing helper or template before writing code.
- Make the smallest change that fixes the root cause. Reuse existing code,
  browser APIs, and installed dependencies before adding anything.
- Do not add speculative abstractions, packages, build tools, routes, IDs, or
  generated files. Delete duplication when safe.
- Keep routes, file names, IDs, and folder structure stable.
- Do not edit `dist/` when a source file exists. Run the existing build instead.

## Allowed scope

- Teaching text, translations, images, PDFs, content JSON, HTML, CSS, and
  browser-only simulation interaction.
- Non-personal local UI preferences such as language, theme, panel state, or
  unfinished local practice, using a subject-prefixed key.

## Protected integration seam

Never change authentication, analytics, tracking, data passing, or deployment.
This includes Supabase, `uni-tracker.js`, `postMessage`, `uniplus:*` events,
identity/session fields, `fetch`, XHR, `sendBeacon`, WebSocket, external
scripts/APIs, `functions/`, `supabase/`, `.github/workflows/`, middleware,
redirects, CSP/CORS, access gates, production URLs, secrets, and settings.

Interactive tools must stay browser-only, self-contained, and must not send
identity, scores, progress, clicks, answers, or telemetry anywhere.

## Before push

For every UI or interaction change:

1. Review the diff. Confirm every file is in scope and no protected term or
   network call was added.
2. Run the repository build or validation command.
3. Open the affected page locally at desktop and tablet widths.
4. Exercise every changed button, link, input, and keyboard path. Assert each
   produces visible output or the expected navigation within a bounded wait.
5. Check accessible names, labels, focus order, keyboard activation, visible
   focus, and console errors.

Do not push or claim the change is ready if any check fails. If no suitable
automated seam exists, report that instead of adding a fake passing test.
